\tag{fdip}
\title{A finite Hurwitz matter sum}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The two loops of a one-vertex cellular torus can carry
the noncommuting quaternion units of \ref{fdip-00SN}.
There are only #{576} ordered choices of two Hurwitz-unit
links, but each acts on all #{16} cochain coefficients.
How does integrating those coefficients change the mean
trace around a loop and the paired field transported along it?}

\transclude{fdip-00Z8}
